<section class="letter" id="welcome">
<div class="letter-text">
<h2>The way in is the way out...</h2>
<p>The Internet can sometimes feel like a giant maze, with websites and apps doing everything they can to suck us in and make us forget our path. I'm happy to tell you that <em>Nibbidā</em> has the exact opposite purpose. It's all about disenchantment here, and no money is involved. If you can find any useful information here in minutes or less, I've done my job correctly.</p>
<h2>...and the way out is through.</h2>
<p>This site is for "insiders". For people who want to delve deep into their own minds. People who, like the Buddha, have seen that there <em>is</em> a way out of the labyrinth, if we allow ourselves to walk through it with increasing clarity and wisdom. The main method for this progress is, of course, meditation. So that's the kind of cultivation and practice that forms the main focus here. But there's a lot more that's helpful to know about the path to liberation...</p>
<p>I hope you like this initiative, and maybe even want to contribute to one of the projects here. May the site make your own exploration of meditation and Dhamma easier, perhaps even more fruitful.</p>
<p>Warmly welcome!</p>
<p class="sign"><em>/Jayadhamma Bhikkhu</em></p>
</div>
<figure class="letter-fig"><img src="{{ '/assets/images/start-cat.jpg' | url }}" width="1208" height="1133" alt="A long-haired cat with closed eyes, rainbow light falling across its face and body" loading="lazy"></figure>
</section>
